🚀 EXECUTE PUSH TO GITHUB
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

OPTION A: Automated Script (Recommended)
───────────────────────────────────────────

  cd /home/claude/p2p-60-24-evo
  bash PUSH_TO_GITHUB.sh

  This script:
  ✓ Verifies repository state
  ✓ Configures git user
  ✓ Sets up GitHub remote
  ✓ Attempts push (SSH first, fallback to HTTPS)
  ✓ Provides manual instructions if auth needed


OPTION B: Manual Push (SSH Key)
───────────────────────────────────────────

  1. Ensure SSH key configured:
     ssh-keygen -t ed25519 -C "your@email.com"
     ssh-add ~/.ssh/id_ed25519

  2. Add public key to GitHub:
     https://github.com/settings/keys
     Copy from: cat ~/.ssh/id_ed25519.pub

  3. Test SSH connection:
     ssh -T git@github.com

  4. Push code:
     cd /home/claude/p2p-60-24-evo
     git push -u origin main

  5. Verify:
     https://github.com/P2P-60-24/p2p-60-24-evo ✅


OPTION C: Manual Push (HTTPS + PAT)
───────────────────────────────────────────

  1. Create Personal Access Token:
     GitHub → Settings → Developer Settings → Personal Access Tokens
     Scope: repo (full control of private repositories)

  2. Configure HTTPS remote:
     cd /home/claude/p2p-60-24-evo
     git remote set-url origin https://github.com/P2P-60-24/p2p-60-24-evo.git

  3. Push code:
     git push -u origin main

  4. When prompted:
     Username: your-github-login
     Password: paste-your-PAT-here

  5. Verify:
     https://github.com/P2P-60-24/p2p-60-24-evo ✅


